Store a new version of a secret and make it current
(POST /v1/vault/secrets/{name}/versions).

Existing bindings keep working and start resolving to the new value; nothing has
to be recreated. Without --host the recorded allowed-hosts list is kept.

The value is read from --value-file or stdin, as with "vault create".

Usage:
  anona-compute vault rotate <name> [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help                help for rotate
      --host stringArray    replace the allowed hosts as well (repeatable)
      --value-file string   file holding the new value ("-" or omitted reads stdin)

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output: one object per line on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
